// One driver for a whole batch: the builders of the briefs the supervisor
// writes, until an escalation.
//
//     nikaia run scripts/drive.nika -- DIR [--max N] [--no-bump] [--ignore-ci-red] [--dry-run] [--lines FILE]
//     nikaia run scripts/drive.nika -- --focus [--max N] [--ignore-ci-red] [--dry-run]
//
// `--focus` (owner, 2026-11-01) rotates through the areas of
// docs/briefs/focus.txt (`block N`, `area NAME DIR` lines, `current NAME
// COUNT`): up to `block` builder briefs of the current area, then the block
// ends (also on BATCH DONE): the suite, a line in docs/briefs/focus-log.md
// (`drive_focus_line`), a pending bump of each area's DIR while CI is green,
// the next area, focus.txt written (not committed). CUT and RED stop for the supervisor as
// in single-DIR mode; an area entered with an empty queue is skipped (`FOCUS
// <area> empty, skipped`); every area empty escalates. Before a block, the first unrun
// docs/briefs/bugs brief with a `Blocks:` line runs first. Test flags:
// `--focus-next FILE [SKIPPED...]`, `--focus-log DIR AREA BRIEF...`,
// `--blocks DIR`.
//
// Loops on `cycle.nika -- DIR` and acts on its lines, one agent at a time:
//
//     NEXT <brief> ...            the brief posted on its issue (once, the
//                                 marker <brief>.posted), agent.nika --
//                                 <brief> --dir DIR; the run's files stay
//                                 untracked; no suite until the batch ends
//     BUMP pending, CI green      cycle.nika -- DIR --apply
//     CUT, RED, BATCH DONE        the batch's suite runs and is waited for,
//                                 then the driver stops for the supervisor
//                                 (`ESCALATE <stop line>: the supervisor
//                                 writes the next briefs`, exit 2); the
//                                 supervisor writes the briefs (a fix-forward
//                                 for RED) and starts the driver again
//
// Output: one line per agent run (`builder done ...`).
// Escalation: one final line, exit 2, on an OWNER line, an ESCALATE of
// agent.nika, a stop line (above), `--max` agent runs (default 8), a push
// rejected after one merge, a suite still red after 2 QA rounds. A RED line
// with a builder queued goes on with it (the supervisor's fix-forward brief).
//
// `--ignore-ci-red`: a RED line of the cycle (CI red on develop) does not
// stop the driver; NEXT and BATCH DONE go on as if CI were green, and a BUMP
// still waits for green CI (a lane whose pushes its own suite gates does not
// fix other lanes' reds; the main lane runs without it).
//
// **Builders commit, the driver tests and pushes** (owner, 2026-10-31: once
// per batch). The driver commits nothing under docs/briefs/ (#1252): briefs,
// reports, run files, focus.txt and the focus log stay untracked working
// files beside the tree. After each builder run, the
// run's brief is appended to DIR/unpushed.txt (one brief path a line). The
// builders of a batch run one after the other with no suite between them. When
// the batch ends (CUT, RED or BATCH DONE) the suite starts on HEAD in the
// background (`drive_suite`); before the next batch's first builder, a bump, or the end of
// the run (an escalation and a RESTART too) the driver waits for it
// (`drive_settle`: one line `SUITE <sha8> waiting`, a poll every 10 s) and
// handles its result. When `git rev-list --count origin/develop..HEAD` is 0
// after a fetch, there is nothing to test (unpushed.txt is emptied). When every
// path those commits touch (`git log --format= --name-only origin/develop..HEAD`)
// is documentation by the rule of scripts/ci-changes.sh (`drive_docs_path`: CI
// skips its build and test jobs for them too), HEAD is pushed as on green
// without a suite, `SUITE <sha8> docs-only, pushed without the suite`, and
// unpushed.txt is emptied. `--docs-only FILE` prints `docs`/`code` for each
// path in FILE and `docs-only` or `suite` (for tests). Else the driver
// takes the checkout's suite lock, `mkdir target/suite.lock` with
// `<pid> <DIR>` in target/suite.lock/owner: two drivers (the main lane and the
// bug lane) share this checkout, so one waits in 60 s steps while the owner's
// pid lives; a dead owner's lock is taken over. Once it has the lock, and
// before each suite run, it fetches and counts again: the other lane's push
// often already holds these commits, and then it prints `SUITE nothing new
// after the lock`, empties unpushed.txt and releases the lock. The lock is held
// through the whole red -> QA -> suite loop (one QA at a time in the
// checkout) and released on every path, an escalation
// too. It notes the tested sha and has CI run the suite (owner, 2026-11-01):
// `git push --force origin <sha>:refs/heads/ci/<lane>`, the last part of the
// lane's DIR (ci/briefs for docs/briefs/), runs the whole workflow nikaia.yml
// on exactly the tested commit, never the shared checkout's unfinished files,
// and nothing of it on this machine's small disk. A rejected push escalates,
// the lock released and the commits left local. Then, detached from the driver
// (`sh -c '( ... ) &'`), `<exe> run scripts/drive.nika -- --ci-wait <sha>
// DIR/suite.log target/suite.lock/exit-<sha>` waits for that run: `gh api
// repos/.../actions/runs?head_sha=<sha>` every 30 s, the workflow Nikaia on a
// ci/ branch; success writes `Gate: green`, any other conclusion `Gate: red
// <failed jobs>` (spaces as `_`) and each failed job's last 200 log lines; no
// run after 15 minutes is `Gate: red ci-no-run`, none finished after 3 hours
// `Gate: red ci-timeout`. Its output goes to DIR/suite.log of the shared
// checkout (overwritten), its exit status to target/suite.lock/exit-<sha>, and
// target/suite.lock/testing notes `<sha> <N>`, N the lines of unpushed.txt the
// tested sha covers; the driver prints `SUITE <sha8> started on CI (<branch>)`,
// and when it has waited, `SUITE <sha8> green|red <steps>`. A develop push of a
// sha CI already passed on a ci/ branch skips the heavy jobs (nikaia.yml).
// Green: `git push origin <sha>:develop`, exactly the tested commit; when
// rejected (other sessions push too), `git merge --autostash` of
// `origin/develop` and push HEAD: the merge is CI's to judge (a merge, not a
// rebase, 2026-11-05: a rebase replays the tested commits). Still rejected:
// escalate. A conflicted merge is never left open in the shared checkout (2026-10-31: both
// lanes write docs/briefs/, and the checkout stayed mid-rebase until fixed by
// hand): the conflicted paths are noted, `git merge --abort` (HEAD and the
// autostash restored), and `ESCALATE drive: push rejected, merge conflicted in
// <paths>, merge aborted`; an abort that fails, or leaves a merge or an
// unmerged path, escalates with `merge left open: ...`. Then it prints
// `PUSHED <sha8>` and drops the N tested lines from unpushed.txt (after a
// merged push of HEAD it empties the file). Red: DIR/qa-input.txt gets the
// suite's step lines, the whole suite.log (the failed jobs' log tails), `git log
// origin/develop..HEAD`, and the brief and report of each brief in
// unpushed.txt; the QA agent runs (role `qa`) on DIR/qa/qa-task.md, a copy of
// the template docs/briefs/qa-task.md made before each run (its report path
// made the copy's), in the shared checkout; the copy, its report and run files
// stay untracked, and the suite runs
// again on the new HEAD, on CI the same way, and is waited for at
// once (the next batch starts only on green). At most 2 QA
// rounds: a third red prints `ESCALATE drive: suite red after 2 QA rounds:
// <steps>` and leaves the commits local. Nothing else pushes.
// `--no-bump` leaves the version raise to another driver: a second lane in the
// same session (`docs/briefs/bugs`) runs with it, so only the main lane's
// driver raises the version and two raises never meet in `CHANGELOG.md`.
// `--dry-run` runs one step of the loop and prints the commands it would run
// and the final line `DRY-RUN <action>`; `--lines FILE` takes the cycle's
// output from FILE instead of running `cycle.nika` (for tests).
// A builder's `Pushed: rejected` (or `none`) is rewritten when its commit is found in the log.
// `--rewrite REPORT LOGFILE` prints the rewritten report (for tests).
// `--issue NAME...` prints each brief's issue number (drive_issue) or `none`;
// `--post-body BRIEF` prints the comment that posts BRIEF (for tests).
// `nikaia run` compiles this script once, so a commit to it does nothing until a
// restart: at the top of each round of a real run the driver reads
// scripts/drive.nika again, and if it changed since the start it prints the one
// final line `RESTART drive: scripts/drive.nika changed` and exits 3 (the main
// session starts it again at once). `--changed OLDFILE` prints that line or
// `same` (for tests).
// The scripts are run as programs: a script cannot `use` another.

use std::cli
use std::env
use std::fs
use std::process
use std::text

fn drive_exe() -> String throws {
    for exe in ["target/fast/nikaia", "target/release/nikaia"] {
        if fs::exists(exe, fs::Root::Anywhere) { return exe.to_string() }
    }
    return ""
}

// Ends the run with exit 2; a suite still running is waited for and handled
// first (drive_settle), with one line naming the escalation it delays.
fn drive_escalate(why: String) throws {
    let lane = drive_lock_lane()
    if lane != "" && drive_testing() != "" {
        println(f"SUITE before escalating: {why}")
        let exe = drive_exe()
        drive_settle(exe.clone(), lane)
    }
    drive_unlock()
    println(f"ESCALATE drive: {why}")
    process::exit(2)
}

// The suite lock of this checkout (drive_suite).
fn drive_lock_dir() -> String {
    return "target/suite.lock"
}

// This driver's pid: the parent of the shell it starts.
fn drive_pid() -> String throws {
    return process::run("sh", ["-c", "echo $PPID"]).stdout.trim().clone()
}

// Releases the suite lock if this driver holds it; every exit path calls it.
fn drive_unlock() throws {
    let owner = drive_read(drive_lock_dir() + "/owner")
    if owner == "" { return }
    if owner.split(" ").collect()[0].trim() == drive_pid() { process::run("rm", ["-rf", drive_lock_dir()]) }
}

// Takes the suite lock: waits in 60 s steps while another live driver holds
// it, takes over a dead one's. An owner file not yet written counts as live
// for two steps.
fn drive_lock(dir: String) throws {
    let me = drive_pid()
    let mut blank: i64 = 0
    let mut said = false
    while true {
        process::run("mkdir", ["-p", "target"])
        if process::run("mkdir", [drive_lock_dir()]).ok {
            fs::write(drive_lock_dir() + "/owner", fs::Root::Anywhere, f"{me} {dir}\n")
            return
        }
        let owner = drive_read(drive_lock_dir() + "/owner").trim().clone()
        let pid = owner.split(" ").collect()[0].clone()
        if pid == "" { blank += 1 }
        let live = if pid == "" { blank <= 2 } else { process::run("kill", ["-0", pid.clone()]).ok }
        if !live {
            process::run("rm", ["-rf", drive_lock_dir()])
            continue
        }
        if !said {
            println(f"SUITE waiting for target/suite.lock: {owner}")
            said = true
        }
        process::run("sleep", ["60"])
    }
}

// The brief's name: the last path component without `.md`.
fn drive_stem(path: String) -> String throws {
    let parts = path.split("/").collect()
    let last = parts[parts.len() - 1].clone()
    return last.replace(".md", "")
}

// The first word of the value after `key:` in a report, "" if absent.
fn drive_field(body: String, key: String) -> String {
    let prefix = key.clone() + ":"
    for line in body.split("\n") {
        let t = line.trim()
        if t.starts_with(prefix.clone()) { return (t.strip_prefix(prefix.clone()) ?? "").trim().clone() }
    }
    return ""
}

fn drive_word(value: String) -> String {
    return value.split(" ").collect()[0].replace(".", "").clone()
}

// Which action a cycle's output leads to, as one line:
//   ESCALATE <why> | STOP <line> | BUMP | NEXT <abs brief>
// STOP (CUT, BATCH DONE, or RED with no builder queued): the driver stops for
// the supervisor, who writes the next briefs. A RED with a builder queued goes
// on with it (the supervisor's fix-forward brief).
// `ignore_red` (--ignore-ci-red): a RED line leads nowhere; NEXT and BATCH DONE
// go on as if CI were green, and BUMP still waits for a green CI line.
fn drive_action(lines: Vec[String], ignore_red: bool) -> String {
    let mut ci: String = ""
    let mut red: String = ""
    let mut batch: String = ""
    let mut bump: String = ""
    for i in 0..<lines.len() {
        let l = lines[i].trim().clone()
        if l.starts_with("OWNER ") { return f"ESCALATE {l}" }
        if l.starts_with("CI ") { ci = l.clone() }
        if l.starts_with("RED ") { red = l.clone() }
        if l.starts_with("NEXT ") || l.starts_with("CUT") || l.starts_with("BATCH") { batch = l.clone() }
        if l.starts_with("BUMP pending") { bump = l.clone() }
    }
    if red != "" && !ignore_red && !batch.starts_with("NEXT ") { return f"STOP {red}" }
    if bump != "" && ci.ends_with("green") && !batch.starts_with("NEXT ") { return "BUMP" }
    if batch.starts_with("NEXT ") { return f"NEXT {batch.split(" ").collect()[1]}" }
    if batch.starts_with("CUT") || batch.starts_with("BATCH DONE") { return f"STOP {batch}" }
    return f"ESCALATE no action for: {batch}"
}

// The report with `Pushed:` rewritten when `Result: done`, `Pushed:` is
// `rejected` or `none`, and a log line `<sha>\t<subject>` has the report's
// `Commit:` as its subject; else the report as it is. The log is the last 40
// commits of both `HEAD` and `origin/develop` (drive_report_pushed), so a commit
// already on `origin/develop` is found too.
fn drive_rewrite(report: String, log: String) -> String {
    if drive_word(drive_field(report.clone(), "Result")) != "done" { return report }
    let pushed = drive_word(drive_field(report.clone(), "Pushed"))
    if pushed != "rejected" && pushed != "none" { return report }
    let subject = drive_field(report.clone(), "Commit")
    if subject == "" { return report }
    let mut sha: String = ""
    for l in log.split("\n") {
        let parts = l.split("\t").collect()
        if sha == "" && parts.len() == 2 && parts[1].trim() == subject { sha = parts[0].trim().clone() }
    }
    if sha == "" { return report }
    let mut out: Vec[String] = []
    let mut done = false
    for l in report.split("\n") {
        if !done && l.trim().starts_with("Pushed:") {
            out.push(f"Pushed: {sha} (pushed by drive.nika)")
            done = true
        } else {
            out.push(l.clone())
        }
    }
    return out.join("\n")
}

fn drive_say(dry: bool, line: String) {
    if dry { println(f"would run: {line}") }
}

// Pushes the tested commit; rejected, merges `origin/develop` once and pushes
// HEAD (the merge is CI's to judge; a merge, not a rebase: a rebase replays the
// tested commits and, on 2026-11-05, deleted every brief a replayed commit had
// untracked). Prints `PUSHED <sha8>`. True when HEAD was pushed (after the
// merge), false when exactly `sha`.
fn drive_push(sha: String) -> bool throws {
    let first = process::run("git", ["push", "origin", f"{sha}:develop"])
    let mut pushed = sha.clone()
    let mut head = false
    if !first.ok {
        // The shared checkout holds other agents' unfinished files and build locks:
        // they are stashed around the merge, not a reason to stop (2026-10-28).
        let fetched = process::run("git", ["fetch", "-q", "origin", "develop"])
        if !fetched.ok { drive_escalate("push rejected, and git fetch origin develop failed") }
        let merged = process::run("git", ["merge", "-q", "--no-edit", "--autostash", "FETCH_HEAD"])
        if !merged.ok { drive_merge_abort() }
        let second = process::run("git", ["push", "origin", "HEAD:develop"])
        if !second.ok { drive_escalate("push rejected after one merge") }
        pushed = process::run("git", ["rev-parse", "HEAD"]).stdout.trim().clone()
        head = true
    }
    println(f"PUSHED {drive_short(pushed)}")
    return head
}

// A failed merge must not leave the shared checkout mid-merge: the conflicted
// paths are noted, `git merge --abort` restores HEAD and applies the autostash
// back, and the check that no merge is left open and no path is unmerged
// precedes the escalation. Always escalates.
fn drive_merge_abort() throws {
    let unmerged = process::run("git", ["diff", "--name-only", "--diff-filter=U"]).stdout.trim().split("\n").collect().join(" ")
    let paths = if unmerged == "" { "no unmerged path" } else { unmerged.clone() }
    let git_dir = process::run("git", ["rev-parse", "--git-dir"]).stdout.trim().clone()
    let mut why: String = ""
    let mut aborted = true
    if fs::exists(f"{git_dir}/MERGE_HEAD", fs::Root::Anywhere) {
        let abort = process::run("git", ["merge", "--abort"])
        aborted = abort.ok
        why = (abort.stderr + abort.stdout).trim().split("\n").collect()[0].clone()
    }
    let open = fs::exists(f"{git_dir}/MERGE_HEAD", fs::Root::Anywhere)
    let left = process::run("git", ["diff", "--name-only", "--diff-filter=U"]).stdout.trim().clone()
    if !aborted || open || left != "" {
        drive_escalate(f"merge left open: push rejected, merge conflicted in {paths}, and git merge --abort did not finish ({why}); the shared checkout needs a hand now")
    }
    drive_escalate(f"push rejected, merge conflicted in {paths}, merge aborted")
}

fn drive_short(sha: String) -> String throws {
    if sha.len() <= 8 { return sha }
    return sha.bytes[0..<8].text().clone()
}

fn drive_append(path: String, line: String) throws {
    let old = drive_read(path.clone())
    let mut text = old.clone()
    if text != "" && !text.ends_with("\n") { text = text + "\n" }
    fs::write(path, fs::Root::Anywhere, text + line + "\n")
}

// The last `n` lines of a text.
fn drive_tail(body: String, n: i64) -> String throws {
    let lines = body.trim_end().split("\n").collect()
    let mut from: i64 = 0
    if lines.len() > n { from = lines.len() - n }
    let mut out: Vec[String] = []
    for i in from..<lines.len() { out.push(lines[i].clone()) }
    return out.join("\n")
}

// What the QA agent reads: the CI run's step lines and suite.log (the failed
// jobs' log tails), the unpushed commits, and the briefs and reports of the
// batch, found from DIR/unpushed.txt among the working files (they are never committed).
fn drive_qa_input(dir: String, out: String, steps: String) throws {
    let mut lines: Vec[String] = []
    lines.push(f"The suite (the CI run on {drive_ci_branch(dir.clone())}, the whole workflow) is red: {steps}")
    lines.push("")
    lines.push("Step lines:")
    for l in out.split("\n") {
        for step in ["CI run ", "no CI run ", "the CI run ", "Gate: "] {
            if l.starts_with(step) { lines.push(l.clone()) }
        }
    }
    lines.push("")
    lines.push(f"{dir}/suite.log (the last 200 lines of each failed job):")
    lines.push(out.trim().clone())
    lines.push("")
    lines.push("Unpushed commits (origin/develop..HEAD; briefs and reports are never among them):")
    lines.push(process::run("git", ["log", "--format=%h %s", "origin/develop..HEAD"]).stdout.trim().clone())
    lines.push("")
    lines.push(f"Briefs and reports of this batch ({dir}/unpushed.txt, untracked working files):")
    for b in drive_read(f"{dir}/unpushed.txt").split("\n") {
        let brief = b.trim().clone()
        if brief == "" { continue }
        lines.push(brief.clone())
        let stem = (brief.strip_suffix(".md") ?? "").clone()
        for r in [f"{brief}.report.md", f"{stem}.report.md"] {
            if r != ".report.md" && fs::exists(r.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere) { lines.push(r.clone()) }
        }
    }
    fs::write(f"{dir}/qa-input.txt", fs::Root::Anywhere, lines.join("\n") + "\n")
}

// The red steps of a gate run, "" when green.
fn drive_red_steps(out: String) -> String throws {
    for l in out.split("\n") {
        if l.starts_with("Gate: green") { return "" }
        if l.starts_with("Gate: red") { return (l.strip_prefix("Gate: red") ?? "").trim().clone() }
    }
    return "gate-error"
}

// The repository CI runs on (the `gh api` paths of drive_ci_wait).
fn drive_repo() -> String {
    return "Nikaia-Foundation/Nikaia"
}

// The branch lane DIR's suite runs on: `ci/` and the last part of DIR
// (docs/briefs -> ci/briefs), so the two lanes never cancel each other's run.
fn drive_ci_branch(dir: String) -> String {
    let parts = dir.trim_end_matches("/").split("/").collect()
    return "ci/" + parts[parts.len() - 1].clone()
}

// Starts one suite run on CI (owner, 2026-11-01): the tested sha is pushed with
// force to the lane's branch `ci/<lane>` (drive_ci_branch), whose push runs the
// whole workflow .github/workflows/nikaia.yml; a waiter detached from the driver
// (`--ci-wait`) follows that run and writes `Gate: green` or `Gate: red <jobs>`
// with the failed jobs' log tails to DIR/suite.log, then the exit status to
// target/suite.lock/exit-<sha>; target/suite.lock/testing notes `<sha> <lines
// of unpushed.txt it covers>` (drive_settle reads both). Nothing builds or tests
// in this checkout.
fn drive_launch(dir: String) throws {
    let sha = process::run("git", ["rev-parse", "HEAD"]).stdout.trim().clone()
    let branch = drive_ci_branch(dir.clone())
    let log = process::run("realpath", [dir.clone()]).stdout.trim().clone() + "/suite.log"
    let exit = process::run("realpath", [drive_lock_dir()]).stdout.trim().clone() + f"/exit-{sha}"
    process::run("rm", ["-f", exit.clone(), log.clone()])
    let mut covered: i64 = 0
    for l in drive_read(f"{dir}/unpushed.txt").split("\n") {
        if l.trim() != "" { covered += 1 }
    }
    let pushed = process::run("git", ["push", "--force", "--quiet", "origin", f"{sha}:refs/heads/{branch}"])
    if !pushed.ok { drive_escalate(f"git push origin {drive_short(sha.clone())}:{branch} failed: {pushed.stderr.trim()}") }
    let bin = drive_exe()
    let exe = process::run("realpath", [bin.clone()]).stdout.trim().clone()
    let script = process::run("realpath", ["scripts/drive.nika"]).stdout.trim().clone()
    let wait = f"'{exe}' run '{script}' -- --ci-wait {sha} '{log}' '{exit}'"
    let started = process::run("sh", ["-c", f"( {wait} ) < /dev/null > /dev/null 2>&1 &"])
    if !started.ok { drive_escalate(f"the CI waiter did not start: {started.stderr.trim()}") }
    fs::write(drive_lock_dir() + "/testing", fs::Root::Anywhere, f"{sha} {covered}\n")
    println(f"SUITE {drive_short(sha)} started on CI ({branch})")
}

// `--ci-wait SHA LOG EXIT`: follows the CI run of the push of SHA to a `ci/`
// branch, polling `gh api` every 30 s. Green writes `Gate: green` to LOG; red
// (failure, cancelled, timed out) writes `Gate: red <job names>` and the last
// 200 lines of each failed job's log; no run after 15 minutes is `Gate: red
// ci-no-run`, none finished after 3 hours `Gate: red ci-timeout`. Then the exit
// status (0 green, 1 red) to EXIT, through EXIT.tmp.
fn drive_ci_wait(sha: String, log: String, exit: String) throws {
    let (body, green) = drive_ci_poll(sha)
    fs::write(log.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere, body)
    let code = if green { "0" } else { "1" }
    fs::write(exit.clone() + ".tmp", fs::Root::Anywhere, code + "\n")
    process::run("mv", [exit.clone() + ".tmp", exit])
}

// One CI verdict for SHA: the log text and whether it is green.
fn drive_ci_poll(sha: String) -> (String, bool) throws {
    let repo = drive_repo()
    let query = ".workflow_runs[] | select(.name == \"Nikaia\" and (.head_branch | startswith(\"ci/\"))) | \"\\(.id) \\(.status) \\(.conclusion)\""
    let mut polls: i64 = 0
    while true {
        let runs = process::run("gh", ["api", f"repos/{repo}/actions/runs?head_sha={sha}&event=push&per_page=20", "--jq", query.clone()])
        let first = runs.stdout.trim().split("\n").collect()[0].trim().clone()
        let words = first.split(" ").collect()
        if runs.ok && words.len() >= 3 && words[1] == "completed" {
            let id = words[0].clone()
            let url = f"https://github.com/{repo}/actions/runs/{id}"
            if words[2] == "success" {
                return (f"CI run {url}: success\nGate: green\n", true)
            } else {
                let jobs = process::run("gh", ["api", f"repos/{repo}/actions/runs/{id}/jobs?per_page=100", "--jq", ".jobs[] | select(.conclusion == \"failure\" or .conclusion == \"cancelled\" or .conclusion == \"timed_out\") | \"\\(.id) \\(.name)\""])
                let mut names: Vec[String] = []
                let mut tails: String = ""
                for j in jobs.stdout.trim().split("\n") {
                    let line = j.trim().clone()
                    if line == "" { continue }
                    let jid = line.split(" ").collect()[0].clone()
                    let name = (line.strip_prefix(jid.clone()) ?? "").trim().clone()
                    names.push(name.replace(" ", "_"))
                    let text = process::run("gh", ["api", f"repos/{repo}/actions/jobs/{jid}/logs"]).stdout
                    tails = tails + f"\nLast 200 lines of the job {name} ({url}/job/{jid}):\n" + drive_tail(text, 200) + "\n"
                }
                if names.len() == 0 { names.push(words[2].clone()) }
                return (f"CI run {url}: {words[2]}\n{tails}\nGate: red " + names.join(" ") + "\n", false)
            }
        }
        if polls >= 30 && first == "" {
            return (f"no CI run for {sha} after 15 minutes\nGate: red ci-no-run\n", false)
        }
        if polls >= 360 {
            return (f"the CI run for {sha} did not finish in 3 hours: {first}\nGate: red ci-timeout\n", false)
        }
        polls += 1
        process::run("sleep", ["30"])
    }
}

// The suite this driver started and has not handled yet: `<sha> <covered>`
// from target/suite.lock/testing while it holds the lock, else "".
fn drive_testing() -> String throws {
    let owner = drive_read(drive_lock_dir() + "/owner")
    if owner == "" || owner.split(" ").collect()[0].trim() != drive_pid() { return "" }
    return drive_read(drive_lock_dir() + "/testing").trim().clone()
}

// The lane directory of the lock this driver holds, "" when it holds none.
fn drive_lock_lane() -> String throws {
    let owner = drive_read(drive_lock_dir() + "/owner").trim().clone()
    let words = owner.split(" ").collect()
    if words.len() < 2 || words[0].trim() != drive_pid() { return "" }
    return words[1].trim().clone()
}

// The QA task's one text; each lane's QA runs on a copy of it (drive_qa_copy).
fn drive_qa_template() -> String {
    return "docs/briefs/qa-task.md"
}

// The brief lane DIR's QA runs on: DIR/qa/qa-task.md, so each lane's QA
// writes its report and run files into its own directory and two drivers'
// commits of them never conflict (2026-10-31: `rebase conflicted in
// docs/briefs/qa-task.md.report.md`).
fn drive_qa_brief(dir: String) -> String {
    return f"{dir}/qa/qa-task.md"
}

// Copies the template to drive_qa_brief(dir), creating DIR/qa/; the one
// change is the report path the template names, made the copy's own.
fn drive_qa_copy(dir: String) throws {
    let qa = drive_qa_brief(dir.clone())
    process::run("mkdir", ["-p", f"{dir}/qa"])
    let text = drive_read(drive_qa_template())
    fs::write(qa.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere, text.replace(f"{drive_qa_template()}.report.md", f"{qa}.report.md"))
}

// Waits for the background suite, if one runs, and handles its result: green
// pushes the tested sha and drops the briefs it covered from unpushed.txt; red
// starts the QA agent, and QA's commit gets its suite at once, waited for, at
// most 2 QA rounds. Releases the lock on every path. One `SUITE <sha8> waiting`
// line, polls every 10 s.
fn drive_settle(exe: String, dir: String) throws {
    let qa = drive_qa_brief(dir.clone())
    let mut rounds: i64 = 0
    while true {
        let testing = drive_testing()
        if testing == "" { return }
        let parts = testing.split(" ").collect()
        let sha = parts[0].clone()
        let mut covered: i64 = 0
        if parts.len() > 1 { covered = text::parse_i64(parts[1].clone()) ?? 0 }
        let exit = f"{drive_lock_dir()}/exit-{sha}"
        if !fs::exists(exit.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere) {
            println(f"SUITE {drive_short(sha.clone())} waiting")
            while !fs::exists(exit.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere) { process::run("sleep", ["10"]) }
        }
        process::run("rm", ["-f", exit, drive_lock_dir() + "/testing"])
        let out = drive_read(f"{dir}/suite.log")
        let steps = drive_red_steps(out.clone())
        if steps == "" {
            println(f"SUITE {drive_short(sha.clone())} green")
            let all = drive_push(sha)
            let mut left: Vec[String] = []
            let mut seen: i64 = 0
            for l in drive_read(f"{dir}/unpushed.txt").split("\n") {
                if l.trim() == "" { continue }
                seen += 1
                if seen > covered && !all { left.push(l.trim().clone()) }
            }
            let mut body: String = ""
            if left.len() > 0 { body = left.join("\n") + "\n" }
            fs::write(f"{dir}/unpushed.txt", fs::Root::Anywhere, body)
            drive_unlock()
            return
        }
        println(f"SUITE {drive_short(sha)} red {steps}")
        if rounds >= 2 { drive_escalate(f"suite red after 2 QA rounds: {steps}") }
        drive_qa_input(dir.clone(), out, steps)
        drive_qa_copy(dir.clone())
        process::run("rm", ["-f", f"{qa}.report.md"])
        drive_agent(exe.clone(), false, dir.clone(), qa.clone(), "qa")
        rounds += 1
        drive_report_pushed(false, qa.clone())
        drive_tidy(false, dir.clone())
        drive_append(f"{dir}/unpushed.txt", qa.clone())
        if drive_nothing_new(dir.clone()) { return }
        drive_launch(dir.clone())
    }
}

// The path rule of scripts/ci-changes.sh (its `docs` output), kept alike with
// it: a path is documentation when it is under guide/ or website/, or ends in
// `.md` and is neither CHANGELOG.md nor under crates/, packages/, examples/,
// benches/, tools/, scripts/, tests/ or docs/specification/. A change of
// .github/workflows/ or of ci-changes.sh itself runs everything.
fn drive_docs_path(path: String) -> bool {
    if path.starts_with("guide/") || path.starts_with("website/") { return true }
    if !path.ends_with(".md") || path == "CHANGELOG.md" { return false }
    for tree in ["crates/", "packages/", "examples/", "benches/", "tools/", "scripts/", "tests/", "docs/specification/"] {
        if path.starts_with(tree) { return false }
    }
    return true
}

// True when every path is documentation (drive_docs_path) and there is one.
fn drive_docs_only(paths: Vec[String]) -> bool {
    let mut any = false
    for p in paths {
        if p == "" { continue }
        if p.starts_with(".github/workflows/") || p == "scripts/ci-changes.sh" { return false }
        if !drive_docs_path(p.clone()) { return false }
        any = true
    }
    return any
}

// The paths the unpushed commits touch, each commit's own.
fn drive_unpushed_paths() -> Vec[String] throws {
    let log = process::run("git", ["log", "--format=", "--name-only", "origin/develop..HEAD"]).stdout
    let mut out: Vec[String] = []
    for line in log.split("\n") {
        let p = line.trim().clone()
        if p != "" { out.push(p) }
    }
    return out
}

// After the lock and before each suite: another lane may have pushed these
// commits meanwhile. Nothing left to push: unpushed.txt emptied, the lock
// released, true.
fn drive_nothing_new(dir: String) -> bool throws {
    process::run("git", ["fetch", "--quiet", "origin", "develop"])
    let count = process::run("git", ["rev-list", "--count", "origin/develop..HEAD"]).stdout.trim().clone()
    if count != "0" { return false }
    fs::write(f"{dir}/unpushed.txt", fs::Root::Anywhere, "")
    drive_unlock()
    println("SUITE nothing new after the lock")
    return true
}

// At the end of a batch: waits for a suite still running (drive_settle), then
// starts the complete suite on HEAD in the background and returns at once
// (header comment).
fn drive_suite(exe: String, dry: bool, dir: String) throws {
    let qa = drive_qa_brief(dir.clone())
    drive_say(dry, "a suite still running (target/suite.lock/testing): wait for it first (SUITE <sha8> waiting)")
    drive_say(dry, "git fetch origin develop; git rev-list --count origin/develop..HEAD (0: nothing to test)")
    drive_say(dry, "git log --format= --name-only origin/develop..HEAD: all documentation by scripts/ci-changes.sh's rule, push HEAD without the suite (SUITE <sha8> docs-only, pushed without the suite), empty " + f"{dir}/unpushed.txt")
    drive_say(dry, "mkdir target/suite.lock (wait while its owner's pid lives)")
    drive_say(dry, "after the lock and before each suite: git fetch origin develop; git rev-list --count origin/develop..HEAD (0: SUITE nothing new after the lock, " + f"empty {dir}/unpushed.txt, rm -rf target/suite.lock)")
    drive_say(dry, f"git push --force origin <sha>:refs/heads/ci/<last part of DIR> (the whole CI workflow runs on that push); in the background: {exe} run scripts/drive.nika -- --ci-wait <sha> {dir}/suite.log target/suite.lock/exit-<sha> (gh api every 30 s; Gate: green, or Gate: red <failed jobs> with their log tails)")
    drive_say(dry, f"before the next batch's first builder (or a bump, or the end): wait for it; green: git push origin <sha>:develop, drop the tested briefs from {dir}/unpushed.txt, rm -rf target/suite.lock")
    drive_say(dry, f"red: write {dir}/qa-input.txt, mkdir -p {dir}/qa, copy {drive_qa_template()} to {qa} (its report path made {qa}.report.md), rm -f {qa}.report.md, {exe} run scripts/agent.nika -- {qa} --dir {dir}, its report and run files stay untracked, the suite again and waited for (at most 2 QA rounds)")
    if dry { return }
    drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
    process::run("git", ["fetch", "--quiet", "origin", "develop"])
    let count = process::run("git", ["rev-list", "--count", "origin/develop..HEAD"]).stdout.trim().clone()
    if count == "0" {
        fs::write(f"{dir}/unpushed.txt", fs::Root::Anywhere, "")
        return
    }
    if drive_docs_only(drive_unpushed_paths()) {
        let head = process::run("git", ["rev-parse", "HEAD"]).stdout.trim().clone()
        println(f"SUITE {drive_short(head.clone())} docs-only, pushed without the suite")
        drive_push(head)
        fs::write(f"{dir}/unpushed.txt", fs::Root::Anywhere, "")
        return
    }
    drive_lock(dir.clone())
    if drive_nothing_new(dir.clone()) { return }
    drive_launch(dir)
}

// After a run: a builder's `Pushed: rejected` (or `none`) is rewritten when
// its commit is found in the log (drive_rewrite). Nothing is committed: the
// brief, its report and run files stay untracked working files beside the
// tree (#1252; owner, 2026-11-05: each such commit started a CI run for nothing).
fn drive_report_pushed(dry: bool, brief: String) throws {
    let report_path = f"{brief}.report.md"
    if !fs::exists(report_path.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere) { return }
    let old = drive_read(report_path.clone())
    if dry {
        drive_say(dry, f"rewrite Pushed: in {report_path} when its Commit: is in the log (nothing committed)")
        return
    }
    process::run("git", ["fetch", "--quiet", "origin", "develop"])
    let log = process::run("git", ["log", "-40", "--format=%h%x09%s", "HEAD", "origin/develop"]).stdout.clone()
    let fresh = drive_rewrite(old.clone(), log)
    if fresh != old { fs::write(report_path, fs::Root::Anywhere, fresh) }
}

// The issue a brief belongs to: the first part of four digits of its name
// after the prefix (`d1-1252-briefs` -> 1252, `b44-1206-x` -> 1206), "" when
// it has none.
fn drive_issue(brief: String) -> String throws {
    let parts = drive_stem(brief).split("-").collect()
    for i in 1..<parts.len() {
        let part = parts[i].clone()
        let mut digits = part.len() == 4
        for c in part.scalars { if !c.is_ascii_digit() { digits = false } }
        if digits { return part }
    }
    return ""
}

// The comment that puts a queued brief on its issue: `Brief queued: <name>`,
// a blank line, the brief, then the generated-by footer.
fn drive_post_body(name: String, text: String) -> String {
    return f"Brief queued: {name}\n\n" + text.trim_end() + "\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n"
}

// Before a brief runs: its text goes as a comment on its issue (drive_issue),
// once; the marker `<brief>.posted` beside it says it did, so a crashed
// session gets the brief back from the issue. No issue, or a failed post, is
// logged (`no issue for <brief>`, `post failed for <brief>`) and the batch goes on.
fn drive_post_brief(dry: bool, brief: String) throws {
    let marker = f"{brief}.posted"
    let name = drive_stem(brief.clone())
    if fs::exists(marker.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere) { return }
    let issue = drive_issue(brief.clone())
    if issue == "" {
        println(f"no issue for {name}")
        return
    }
    let api = f"repos/{drive_repo()}/issues/{issue}/comments"
    drive_say(dry, f"gh api {api} -F body=@<Brief queued: {name}, the brief, the footer>; write {marker}")
    if dry { return }
    let file = process::run("mktemp", []).stdout.trim().clone()
    fs::write(file.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere, drive_post_body(name.clone(), drive_read(brief)))
    let posted = process::run("gh", ["api", api, "-F", f"body=@{file}"])
    process::run("rm", ["-f", file])
    if !posted.ok {
        println(f"post failed for {name}")
        return
    }
    fs::write(marker, fs::Root::Anywhere, f"{issue}\n")
}

// What a run leaves behind that no commit takes: untracked step reports
// (`*.step<N>.report.md`) beside the briefs.
fn drive_tidy(dry: bool, dir: String) throws {
    let left = process::run("git", ["ls-files", "--others", "--exclude-standard", "--", dir])
    let mut stray: Vec[String] = []
    for l in left.stdout.trim().split("\n") {
        if l.contains(".step") && l.ends_with(".report.md") { stray.push(l.clone()) }
    }
    if stray.len() > 0 { drive_say(dry, "rm -f " + stray.join(" ")) }
    if dry { return }
    for i in 0..<stray.len() { process::run("rm", ["-f", stray[i].clone()]) }
}

// Runs one agent; prints `<role> done ...`; escalates on anything else.
fn drive_agent(exe: String, dry: bool, dir: String, brief: String, role: String) throws {
    drive_say(dry, f"{exe} run scripts/agent.nika -- {brief} --dir {dir}")
    if dry { return }
    let out = process::run(exe, ["run", "scripts/agent.nika", "--", brief.clone(), "--dir", dir.clone()])
    let mut done: String = ""
    let mut first: String = ""
    for l in out.stdout.trim().split("\n") {
        if first == "" { first = l.clone() }
        if l.starts_with("done ") { done = l.clone() }
    }
    if done == "" || !out.ok {
        if first == "" { first = f"agent.nika exited with code {out.code}" }
        drive_escalate(first)
    }
    println(f"{role} {done}")
}

fn drive_read(path: String) -> String throws {
    if !fs::exists(path.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere) { return "" }
    return fs::read_to_string(path, fs::Root::Anywhere)
}

fn drive_cycle(exe: String, dir: String, lines_file: String) -> String throws {
    if lines_file != "" { return drive_read(lines_file) }
    let c = process::run(exe, ["run", "scripts/cycle.nika", "--", dir])
    if !c.ok { drive_escalate("cycle.nika failed") }
    return c.stdout.clone()
}

// One builder run of DIR's brief: the brief posted on its issue (once), the
// agent, its report's `Pushed:` checked, the tidy, the brief appended to
// DIR/unpushed.txt. Nothing under docs/briefs/ is committed.
fn drive_builder(exe: String, dry: bool, dir: String, brief: String) throws {
    drive_say(dry, "a batch's suite still running (target/suite.lock/testing): wait for it and handle it (drive_settle) first")
    drive_post_brief(dry, brief.clone())
    drive_agent(exe.clone(), dry, dir.clone(), brief.clone(), "builder")
    drive_report_pushed(dry, brief.clone())
    drive_tidy(dry, dir.clone())
    drive_say(dry, f"append {brief} to {dir}/unpushed.txt (no suite until the batch ends)")
    if dry { return }
    drive_append(f"{dir}/unpushed.txt", brief.clone())
}

// The batch ends at a stop line: its suite runs and is waited for (pushed when
// green), then the driver stops for the supervisor, who writes the next briefs
// (a fix-forward for RED). A dry run prints `DRY-RUN STOP <stop>`.
fn drive_stop(exe: String, dry: bool, dir: String, stop: String) throws {
    drive_suite(exe.clone(), dry, dir.clone())
    drive_say(dry, "wait for the suite (drive_settle), then stop for the supervisor (exit 2)")
    if dry {
        println(f"DRY-RUN STOP {stop}")
        return
    }
    drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
    drive_unlock()
    println(f"ESCALATE {stop}: the supervisor writes the next briefs")
    process::exit(2)
}

// The words of the first line of a focus file that starts with `key`, empty
// without one. The file (docs/briefs/focus.txt):
//     block 3
//     area bugs docs/briefs/bugs
//     current bugs 0
fn drive_focus_words(text: String, key: String) -> Vec[String] {
    for line in text.split("\n") {
        let words = line.trim().split(" ").collect()
        if words.len() > 1 && words[0] == key { return words }
    }
    let none: Vec[String] = []
    return none
}

// The block length (builder briefs an area runs before the focus moves on), 3
// when the file names none.
fn drive_focus_block(text: String) -> i64 {
    let words = drive_focus_words(text, "block")
    if words.len() < 2 { return 3 }
    return text::parse_i64(words[1].clone()) ?? 3
}

// The areas in order, each `NAME DIR`.
fn drive_focus_areas(text: String) -> Vec[String] {
    let mut out: Vec[String] = []
    for line in text.split("\n") {
        let words = line.trim().split(" ").collect()
        if words.len() == 3 && words[0] == "area" { out.push(words[1].clone() + " " + words[2].clone()) }
    }
    return out
}

// The current area's name: the `current` line's, else the first area's.
fn drive_focus_current(text: String) -> String {
    let words = drive_focus_words(text, "current")
    if words.len() > 1 { return words[1].clone() }
    let areas = drive_focus_areas(text)
    if areas.len() == 0 { return "" }
    return areas[0].split(" ").collect()[0].clone()
}

// The builder runs the current area has had in its block.
fn drive_focus_count(text: String) -> i64 {
    let words = drive_focus_words(text, "current")
    if words.len() < 3 { return 0 }
    return text::parse_i64(words[2].clone()) ?? 0
}

// The directory of area NAME, "" when the file has no such area.
fn drive_focus_dir(text: String, name: String) -> String {
    for area in drive_focus_areas(text) {
        let words = area.split(" ").collect()
        if words[0] == name { return words[1].clone() }
    }
    return ""
}

// `text` with its `current` line set to `NAME COUNT` (appended when absent).
fn drive_focus_set(text: String, name: String, count: i64) -> String {
    let mut out: Vec[String] = []
    let mut set = false
    for line in text.trim_end().split("\n") {
        if line.trim().starts_with("current ") || line.trim() == "current" {
            out.push(f"current {name} {count}")
            set = true
        } else {
            out.push(line.clone())
        }
    }
    if !set { out.push(f"current {name} {count}") }
    return out.join("\n") + "\n"
}

// The area after the current one, wrapping, whose name is not in `skipped`
// (` a b `, the areas found empty in this rotation); the current one itself
// comes last. "" when every area is skipped.
fn drive_focus_next(text: String, skipped: String) -> String {
    let areas = drive_focus_areas(text.clone())
    let current = drive_focus_current(text)
    let n = areas.len()
    let mut at: i64 = 0
    for i in 0..<n {
        if areas[i].split(" ").collect()[0] == current { at = i }
    }
    for k in 0..<n {
        let name = areas[(at + 1 + k) % n].split(" ").collect()[0].clone()
        if !skipped.contains(f" {name} ") { return name }
    }
    return ""
}

// Micro-dollars of "12.34": whole * 1_000_000 + the first six decimals.
fn drive_micro(cost: String) -> i64 throws {
    let parts = cost.trim().split(".").collect()
    let whole = text::parse_i64(parts[0].clone()) ?? 0
    if parts.len() < 2 { return whole * 1000000 }
    let padded = parts[1].clone() + "000000"
    let frac = text::parse_i64(padded.bytes[0..<6].text()) ?? 0
    return whole * 1000000 + frac
}

// The focus log's line of one block: `<stamp> <area> briefs <n> done <d>
// partial <p> blocked <b> noop <o> tokens <t> cost <c> queue <q>`. `tokens`: the rows (`BRIEF TOKENS CALLS`) of the block's
// briefs from tokens.txt; `costs`: the cost.txt lines (`DATE USD`) the block
// added.
fn drive_focus_line(stamp: String, area: String, reports: Vec[String], tokens: Vec[String], costs: Vec[String], queue: i64) -> String throws {
    let mut done = 0
    let mut partial = 0
    let mut blocked = 0
    let mut noop = 0
    for report in reports {
        let result = drive_word(drive_field(report.clone(), "Result"))
        if result == "done" { done += 1 }
        if result == "partial" { partial += 1 }
        if result == "blocked" { blocked += 1 }
        if result == "noop" { noop += 1 }
    }
    let mut sum = 0
    for row in tokens {
        let words = row.trim().split(" ").collect()
        if words.len() > 1 { sum += text::parse_i64(words[1].clone()) ?? 0 }
    }
    let mut micro = 0
    for row in costs {
        let words = row.trim().split(" ").collect()
        if words.len() == 2 { micro += drive_micro(words[1].clone()) }
    }
    let cents = (micro + 5000) / 10000
    let rest = cents % 100
    let pad = if rest < 10 { "0" } else { "" }
    return f"{stamp} {area} briefs {reports.len()} done {done} partial {partial} blocked {blocked} noop {noop} tokens {sum} cost {cents / 100}.{pad}{rest} queue {queue}"
}

// The report of a brief that exists (`BRIEF.report.md`, else the stem's), or "".
fn drive_report_of(brief: String) -> String throws {
    let report = f"{brief}.report.md"
    if fs::exists(report.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere) { return report }
    let stem = (brief.strip_suffix(".md") ?? "").clone()
    if stem != "" && fs::exists(f"{stem}.report.md", fs::Root::Anywhere) { return f"{stem}.report.md" }
    return ""
}

// The briefs of DIR/batch.txt that exist and have no report yet, as paths
// under DIR.
fn drive_unrun(dir: String) -> Vec[String] throws {
    let mut out: Vec[String] = []
    for raw in drive_read(f"{dir}/batch.txt").split("\n") {
        let name = raw.trim().clone()
        if name == "" { continue }
        let brief = f"{dir}/{name}"
        if fs::exists(brief.clone(), fs::Root::Anywhere) && drive_report_of(brief.clone()) == "" { out.push(brief) }
    }
    return out
}

// The first unrun brief of DIR/batch.txt with a `Blocks:` line (a defect that
// holds up a move), as its absolute path; "" when none.
fn drive_focus_blocking(dir: String) -> String throws {
    for brief in drive_unrun(dir) {
        for line in drive_read(brief.clone()).split("\n") {
            if line.trim().starts_with("Blocks:") { return process::run("realpath", [brief.clone()]).stdout.trim().clone() }
        }
    }
    return ""
}

// The lines of a text, a trailing newline not counted.
fn drive_line_count(body: String) -> i64 {
    if body.trim() == "" { return 0 }
    return body.trim_end().split("\n").collect().len()
}

// The focus log line of a block of AREA (DIR) that ran `briefs`: their
// reports, their rows of tokens.txt beside each brief, the lines of
// DIR/cost.txt from line `cost_from` on, the unrun briefs left in DIR.
fn drive_focus_record(stamp: String, area: String, dir: String, briefs: Vec[String], cost_from: i64) -> String throws {
    let mut reports: Vec[String] = []
    let mut tokens: Vec[String] = []
    for brief in briefs {
        let report = drive_report_of(brief.clone())
        if report != "" { reports.push(drive_read(report)) }
        let cut = brief.rfind("/") ?? 0
        let home = if cut > 0 { brief[0..<cut].clone() } else { "." }
        for row in drive_read(f"{home}/tokens.txt").split("\n") {
            if row.trim().split(" ").collect()[0] == brief { tokens.push(row.clone()) }
        }
    }
    let mut costs: Vec[String] = []
    let lines = drive_read(f"{dir}/cost.txt").trim_end().split("\n").collect()
    for i in 0..<lines.len() {
        if i >= cost_from && lines[i].trim() != "" { costs.push(lines[i].clone()) }
    }
    return drive_focus_line(stamp, area, reports, tokens, costs, drive_unrun(dir).len())
}

// The end of a block: the suite (started, then waited for: pushed on green,
// QA on red), the focus log line, the bump of each area's DIR with one pending
// while CI is green, the focus moved to the next area (focus.txt and the log
// are working files, not committed: #1252). `file`: the focus file as read at the block's start.
fn drive_focus_end(exe: String, dry: bool, file: String, area: String, dir: String, briefs: Vec[String], cost_from: i64) throws {
    let path = "docs/briefs/focus.txt"
    let log = "docs/briefs/focus-log.md"
    drive_suite(exe.clone(), dry, dir.clone())
    drive_say(dry, "wait for the suite (drive_settle)")
    drive_say(dry, f"append the block's line to {log}")
    if !dry {
        drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
        let stamp = process::run("date", ["+%F %H:%M"]).stdout.trim().clone()
        let line = drive_focus_record(stamp, area.clone(), dir.clone(), briefs, cost_from)
        drive_append(log, line.clone())
        println(f"FOCUS {line}")
    }
    for each in drive_focus_areas(file.clone()) {
        let other = each.split(" ").collect()[1].clone()
        drive_say(dry, f"{exe} run scripts/cycle.nika -- {other}: BUMP pending and CI green: {exe} run scripts/cycle.nika -- {other} --apply")
        if dry { continue }
        let cyc = drive_cycle(exe.clone(), other.clone(), "")
        let green = cyc.contains(" green\n") || cyc.trim().ends_with(" green")
        if green && cyc.contains("BUMP pending") {
            let rel = process::run(exe.clone(), ["run", "scripts/cycle.nika", "--", other.clone(), "--apply"])
            if rel.stdout.contains("PUSH REJECTED") { drive_escalate("bump push rejected") }
        }
    }
    let next = drive_focus_next(file.clone(), " ")
    drive_say(dry, f"set {path} to current {next} 0 (not committed)")
    if dry { return }
    fs::write(path, fs::Root::Anywhere, drive_focus_set(drive_read(path), next, 0))
}

// `--focus` (owner, 2026-11-01): one driver, one area at a time. Drives the
// current area of docs/briefs/focus.txt as the single-DIR loop does, counting
// its builder runs; the block ends at `block` runs or on BATCH DONE
// (drive_focus_end), and the focus moves to the next area. Before each block
// an unrun bug brief with a `Blocks:` line runs first (it counts for the bugs
// area). An area entered with nothing to run is skipped for this rotation
// (`FOCUS <area> empty, skipped`), and every area empty escalates. RED and CUT
// stop for the supervisor as in the single-DIR loop.
fn drive_focus(exe: String, dry: bool, max: i64, ignore_red: bool, lines_file: String) throws {
    let path = "docs/briefs/focus.txt"
    let bugs = "docs/briefs/bugs"
    let own = drive_read("scripts/drive.nika")
    let mut runs: i64 = 0
    let mut skipped: String = " "
    let mut briefs: Vec[String] = []
    let mut cost_from: i64 = -1
    while true {
        let file = drive_read(path)
        let area = drive_focus_current(file.clone())
        let dir = drive_focus_dir(file.clone(), area.clone())
        if dir == "" { drive_escalate(f"focus: {path} names no area {area}") }
        if !dry && drive_read("scripts/drive.nika") != own {
            drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
            println("RESTART drive: scripts/drive.nika changed")
            process::exit(3)
        }
        let block = drive_focus_block(file.clone())
        let count = drive_focus_count(file.clone())
        if cost_from < 0 { cost_from = drive_line_count(drive_read(f"{dir}/cost.txt")) }
        if dry { println(f"FOCUS {area} {dir} {count} of {block}") }
        // A bug brief that holds up a move goes first, before each block.
        if count == 0 && briefs.len() == 0 {
            let urgent = drive_focus_blocking(bugs)
            if urgent != "" {
                if runs >= max { drive_escalate(f"--max {max} agent runs reached") }
                if !dry && drive_testing() != "" { drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone()) }
                let bugs_from = drive_line_count(drive_read(f"{bugs}/cost.txt"))
                drive_builder(exe.clone(), dry, bugs, urgent.clone())
                runs += 1
                if dry {
                    println(f"DRY-RUN NEXT {drive_stem(urgent)} (Blocks:)")
                    return
                }
                if area == "bugs" {
                    briefs.push(urgent)
                    fs::write(path, fs::Root::Anywhere, drive_focus_set(file, area, 1))
                } else {
                    let stamp = process::run("date", ["+%F %H:%M"]).stdout.trim().clone()
                    let line = drive_focus_record(stamp, "bugs", bugs, [urgent], bugs_from)
                    drive_append("docs/briefs/focus-log.md", line.clone())
                    println(f"FOCUS {line}")
                }
                continue
            }
        }
        let cyc = drive_cycle(exe.clone(), dir.clone(), lines_file.clone())
        let mut lines: Vec[String] = []
        // A bump waits for the end of a block (drive_focus_end).
        for l in cyc.trim().split("\n") {
            if l.trim() != "" && !l.trim().starts_with("BUMP") { lines.push(l.trim().clone()) }
        }
        if lines.len() == 0 { drive_escalate("cycle.nika printed nothing") }
        let action = drive_action(lines.clone(), ignore_red)
        if action.starts_with("ESCALATE ") {
            drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
            drive_unlock()
            println(action)
            process::exit(2)
        }
        if !dry && action.starts_with("NEXT ") && drive_testing() != "" {
            drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
            continue
        }
        if runs >= max { drive_escalate(f"--max {max} agent runs reached") }
        if action.starts_with("NEXT ") {
            let brief = (action.strip_prefix("NEXT ") ?? "").clone()
            drive_builder(exe.clone(), dry, dir.clone(), brief.clone())
            runs += 1
            if dry {
                println(f"DRY-RUN NEXT {drive_stem(brief)}")
                return
            }
            briefs.push(brief)
            fs::write(path, fs::Root::Anywhere, drive_focus_set(file.clone(), area.clone(), count + 1))
            if count + 1 < block { continue }
            drive_focus_end(exe.clone(), dry, file, area, dir, briefs.clone(), cost_from)
            briefs = []
            cost_from = -1
            skipped = " "
            continue
        }
        let stop = (action.strip_prefix("STOP ") ?? "").clone()
        if !stop.starts_with("BATCH DONE") {
            drive_stop(exe.clone(), dry, dir.clone(), stop.clone())
            return
        }
        // BATCH DONE: a block that ran briefs ends here.
        if briefs.len() > 0 {
            if dry { println("DRY-RUN BLOCK END") }
            drive_focus_end(exe.clone(), dry, file, area, dir, briefs.clone(), cost_from)
            if dry { return }
            briefs = []
            cost_from = -1
            skipped = " "
            continue
        }
        // Entered with nothing to run: skipped; the supervisor fills the queue.
        println(f"FOCUS {area} empty, skipped")
        skipped = skipped + area.clone() + " "
        let next = drive_focus_next(file.clone(), skipped.clone())
        if next == "" {
            drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
            drive_unlock()
            println("ESCALATE focus: every area empty")
            process::exit(2)
        }
        fs::write(path, fs::Root::Anywhere, drive_focus_set(file, next, 0))
        cost_from = -1
    }
}

fn main() throws {
    let mut dir: String = ""
    let mut max: i64 = 8
    let mut dry = false
    let mut no_bump = false
    let mut ignore_red = false
    let mut lines_file: String = ""
    let mut focus = false
    let mut args: Vec[String] = []
    for a in cli::args() { args.push(a) }
    let mut i = 1
    while i < args.len() {
        if args[i] == "--dry-run" {
            dry = true
        } else if args[i] == "--ignore-ci-red" {
            ignore_red = true
        } else if args[i] == "--focus" {
            focus = true
        } else if args[i] == "--no-bump" {
            no_bump = true
        } else if args[i] == "--max" && i + 1 < args.len() {
            max = text::parse_i64(args[i + 1].clone()) ?? 8
            i += 1
        } else if args[i] == "--lines" && i + 1 < args.len() {
            lines_file = args[i + 1].clone()
            dry = true
            i += 1
        } else {
            dir = args[i].clone()
        }
        i += 1
    }
    if args.len() >= 3 && args[1] == "--focus-next" {
        let text = drive_read(args[2].clone())
        let mut skipped: String = " "
        for k in 3..<args.len() { skipped = skipped + args[k].clone() + " " }
        let next = drive_focus_next(text.clone(), skipped)
        if next == "" { println("ESCALATE focus: every area empty") } else { print(drive_focus_set(text, next, 0)) }
        return
    }
    if args.len() >= 4 && args[1] == "--focus-log" {
        let mut briefs: Vec[String] = []
        for k in 4..<args.len() { briefs.push(args[k].clone()) }
        println(drive_focus_record("2026-11-01 12:00", args[3].clone(), args[2].clone(), briefs, 0))
        return
    }
    if args.len() >= 2 && args[1] == "--issue" {
        for k in 2..<args.len() {
            let issue = drive_issue(args[k].clone())
            let name = args[k].clone()
            if issue == "" { println(f"{name} none") } else { println(f"{name} {issue}") }
        }
        return
    }
    if args.len() == 3 && args[1] == "--post-body" {
        print(drive_post_body(drive_stem(args[2].clone()), drive_read(args[2].clone())))
        return
    }
    if args.len() == 3 && args[1] == "--blocks" {
        let urgent = drive_focus_blocking(args[2].clone())
        if urgent == "" { println("none") } else { println(drive_stem(urgent)) }
        return
    }
    if focus {
        let exe = drive_exe()
        if exe == "" {
            println("BUILD cargo build --profile fast -p nikaia")
            process::exit(1)
        }
        drive_focus(exe, dry, max, ignore_red, lines_file)
        return
    }
    if dir == "" {
        println("usage: nikaia run scripts/drive.nika -- DIR [--max N] [--no-bump] [--ignore-ci-red] [--dry-run] [--lines FILE]")
        println("       nikaia run scripts/drive.nika -- --focus [--max N] [--dry-run]")
        process::exit(2)
    }
    if args.len() == 4 && args[1] == "--rewrite" {
        println(drive_rewrite(drive_read(args[2].clone()), drive_read(args[3].clone())))
        return
    }
    if args.len() == 5 && args[1] == "--ci-wait" {
        drive_ci_wait(args[2].clone(), args[3].clone(), args[4].clone())
        return
    }
    if args.len() == 3 && args[1] == "--docs-only" {
        let mut paths: Vec[String] = []
        for line in drive_read(args[2].clone()).split("\n") {
            let p = line.trim().clone()
            if p == "" { continue }
            if drive_docs_path(p.clone()) { println(f"docs {p}") } else { println(f"code {p}") }
            paths.push(p)
        }
        if drive_docs_only(paths) { println("docs-only") } else { println("suite") }
        return
    }
    if args.len() == 3 && args[1] == "--changed" {
        if drive_read(args[2].clone()) != drive_read("scripts/drive.nika") {
            println("RESTART drive: scripts/drive.nika changed")
        } else {
            println("same")
        }
        return
    }
    let exe = drive_exe()
    if exe == "" {
        println("BUILD cargo build --profile fast -p nikaia")
        process::exit(1)
    }
    let mut runs: i64 = 0
    let mut bumps: i64 = 0
    let own = drive_read("scripts/drive.nika")
    while runs <= max {
        if !dry && drive_read("scripts/drive.nika") != own {
            drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
            println("RESTART drive: scripts/drive.nika changed")
            process::exit(3)
        }
        let cyc = drive_cycle(exe.clone(), dir.clone(), lines_file.clone())
        let mut lines: Vec[String] = []
        for l in cyc.trim().split("\n") {
            if l.trim() != "" && !(no_bump && l.trim().starts_with("BUMP")) { lines.push(l.trim().clone()) }
        }
        if lines.len() == 0 { drive_escalate("cycle.nika printed nothing") }
        let action = drive_action(lines.clone(), ignore_red)
        if action.starts_with("ESCALATE ") {
            drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
            drive_unlock()
            println(action)
            process::exit(2)
        }
        // A builder of the next batch and a bump wait for the batch's suite, and the cycle is read again (QA may
        // have committed, a push moved CI).
        if !dry && (action.starts_with("NEXT ") || action == "BUMP") && drive_testing() != "" {
            drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
            continue
        }
        // A bump pushes HEAD: commits not yet through the suite (a restart
        // between a batch and its suite leaves them) are tested first.
        if !dry && action == "BUMP" && drive_read(f"{dir}/unpushed.txt").trim() != "" {
            drive_suite(exe.clone(), dry, dir.clone())
            drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir.clone())
            continue
        }
        if action == "BUMP" {
            bumps += 1
            if bumps > 3 { drive_escalate("BUMP pending persists after --apply") }
            drive_say(dry, f"{exe} run scripts/cycle.nika -- {dir} --apply")
            if dry {
                println("DRY-RUN BUMP")
                return
            }
            let rel = process::run(exe.clone(), ["run", "scripts/cycle.nika", "--", dir.clone(), "--apply"])
            if rel.stdout.contains("PUSH REJECTED") { drive_escalate("bump push rejected") }
            continue
        }
        if runs >= max { drive_escalate(f"--max {max} agent runs reached") }
        if action.starts_with("NEXT ") {
            let brief = (action.strip_prefix("NEXT ") ?? "").clone()
            drive_builder(exe.clone(), dry, dir.clone(), brief)
            runs += 1
            if dry {
                println(f"DRY-RUN NEXT {drive_stem(action.clone())}")
                return
            }
            continue
        }
        // CUT, BATCH DONE or RED: stop for the supervisor.
        drive_stop(exe.clone(), dry, dir.clone(), (action.strip_prefix("STOP ") ?? "").clone())
        return
    }
    drive_settle(exe.clone(), dir)
}
